From f6bb8d46ba8b1f8912b6ddf54fa7126281793e19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rob <rob@3adesign.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 20 Mar 2026 11:13:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add MSB-aligned 16-bit pixel format support for 10/12-bit
 depths

Introduces opt-in MSB-aligned (left-justified) input and output format
for 10-bit and 12-bit pixel data. When enabled, pixel value `v` of
depth `d` is stored in the top `d` bits of a uint16_t word
(i.e. `v << (16 - d)`), matching the convention used by many
professional video APIs.

The 8-bit path is unchanged.

API:
  svt_jpeg_xs_encoder_api_t.input_bit_depth_msb_aligned  (default 0)
  svt_jpeg_xs_decoder_api_t.output_bit_depth_msb_aligned (default 0)

Both fields consume one byte from existing struct padding so ABI size
is preserved.

Encoder: the MSB-aligned shift (Bw-16) is constant across all depths,
so the per-pixel AND mask is eliminated entirely. The flag propagates
via picture_header_dynamic.hdr_input_msb_aligned, which is already
threaded through the DWT/NLT call chain, requiring no call-site changes.

Decoder: nlt_inverse_transform_line_16bit gains an msb_aligned param
(one call site). Output functions shift the clamped value left by
(16-depth) before storing.

C, AVX2, and AVX512 implementations provided for both directions.
New tests: Nlt_Linear_Input_16bit_MSB and Nlt_Linear_Output_16bit_MSB
verify correctness against the C reference and assert that output words
have their lower (16-depth) bits zeroed. All 11934 existing tests pass.
